{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And twelve pillars.</b> As it is written, ״and you shall bound the people around.״ Three tribes in the east and three in the south and three in the west and three in the north, in the same order that they were encamped in the wilderness around the Tabernacle. And another interpretation: he set twelve stones in the east, to testify that all of them consented to the covenant, and a precedent for this is found in what Elijah did on Mount Carmel: ״and they took twelve stones, according to the number of the children of Israel.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:09.014845022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}